-# Artefact schemas
-
-Generated by `scripts/schemas.py` — the SAME definition that
-`validate_results` enforces. Editing this file by hand will be overwritten;
-edit `scripts/schemas.py` instead.
-
-## Common envelope
-
-Every JSON artefact written by `_common.write_json` carries:
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `schema` | string | - | the artefact's schema id |
-| `schema_version` | string | - | the experiment-wide schema generation |
-| `written_at` | ISO-8601 UTC | - | when this file was written |
-| `provenance_ref` | object | - | {run_id, file, sha256} pointing at results/provenance.json |
-
-## Authoritative timings
-
-In-script `time.monotonic()` deltas are AUTHORITATIVE. Snakemake's `benchmark:` wall-clock is used for cross-checking only, and its memory / IO columns are literally `0` on this macOS host — reporting them as measurements would be fabrication.
-
-## `results/preregistration.json`
-
-- **schema**: `andamentum.experiment.docstore_deferred.preregistration/1`
-- **produced by**: `prereg`
-- **required keys**: `hypotheses`, `n_hypotheses`
-
-Every hypothesis with its numeric threshold and falsifier, written before any measurement exists. analyze.py may only compare against this file.
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `hypotheses[].id` | string | - | hypothesis id, e.g. H-c2 |
-| `hypotheses[].claim` | string | - | which lettered claim it belongs to |
-| `hypotheses[].threshold` | object|null | - | {metric, op, value} |
-| `hypotheses[].falsifier` | string|null | - | what would flip it |
-
-## `results/provenance.json`
-
-- **schema**: `andamentum.experiment.provenance/1`
-- **produced by**: `provenance`
-- **required keys**: `run_id`, `git`, `machine`, `packages`, `ollama`
-
-Run identity: git, versions, model digests, machine, allowlisted env.
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `run_id` | string | - | '<UTC ISO8601>-<git short sha>' |
-| `ollama.pinned_models.<name>.digest` | string | - | THE load-bearing pin: the tag is mutable, the digest is not |
-| `git.dirty` | bool | - | whether the working tree had uncommitted changes |
-| `environment_allowlisted` | object | - | only DOCUMENT_STORE_DIR / OLLAMA_BASE_URL / TZ / LANG — never the full environ |
-
-## `data/REGISTRY.json`
-
-- **schema**: `andamentum.experiment.docstore_deferred.registry/1`
-- **produced by**: `fetch_pdfs`
-- **required keys**: `papers`, `registry_version`
-
-Per-paper input provenance. Committed; data/pdfs/ is gitignored.
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `papers[].arxiv_id` | string | - | VERSIONED id, e.g. 1706.03762v7 |
-| `papers[].sha256` | hex string | - | content hash of the downloaded PDF |
-| `papers[].bytes` | int | bytes | file size |
-| `papers[].final_url` | string | - | URL after redirects |
-| `papers[].etag` | string|null | - | upstream ETag, when offered |
-| `papers[].download_seconds` | float | s | wall-clock of the fetch |
-
-## `results/data_integrity.json`
-
-- **schema**: `andamentum.experiment.docstore_deferred.data_integrity/1`
-- **produced by**: `verify_registry`
-- **required keys**: `verdict`, `checks`, `n_failed`
-
-Re-hash of every registered PDF. Exits 1 on drift.
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `checks[].ok` | bool | - | sha256 and size both match the registry |
-
-## `results/conversion_baseline.json`
-
-- **schema**: `andamentum.experiment.docstore_deferred.conversion_baseline/1`
-- **produced by**: `convert_reference`
-- **required keys**: `conversions`, `docling_version`
-
-Standalone harvest.extract per PDF: the markdown corpus, and the per-PDF conversion cost that prices the checkpoint.
-
-| field | type | units | meaning |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| `conversions[].conversion_seconds` | float | s | harvest.extract wall-clock |
-| `conversions[].markdown_chars` | int | characters | extracted length |
-| `conversions[].markdown_sha256` | hex string | - | valid WITHIN a docling version only — never compared across runs |
-
-## `results/gate_llm.json`
-
